sections.wikitext:
The music video for the song was released to [[YouTube]] on April 29, 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url =https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Io0fBr1XBUA|title=The Chainsmokers – Don't Let Me Down ft. Daya—Youtube|access-date = April 30, 2016|date = April 29, 2016|work = YouTube}}</ref>

In the video, Andrew Taggart and Alex Pall (the Chainsmokers) get into a yellow [[convertible]], lowrider at sunrise and begin to drive down a wooded mountain road. Intercut with shots of them driving is [[Daya (singer)|Daya]], dressed in black leather pants and jacket, singing in a misty field full of bushes. Taggart and Pall stop the car when Daya, surrounded by dancers dressed similarly to her, stand in the middle of the road, blocking it. Daya sings as the girls perform dance moves around her while Taggart and Pall watch from the car. Suddenly, the cars hydraulic suspension begins bouncing up and down on its wheels. As the beat progresses, the rocking of the car becomes more violent and aggressive. Towards the end of the song, the rocking lifts Taggart and Pall out of the car and they are suspended in the air as the girls disperse.{{Citation needed|date=March 2024}}

As of June 2025, the video has received over 2.2 billion views on YouTube.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Io0fBr1XBUA|title=The Chainsmokers – Don't Let Me Down (Video) ft. Daya|work=YouTube|date=April 29, 2016}}</ref>

